            </note>
            <note corresp="#d556-f2" n="2" xml:id="d556-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed (Willauer papers).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d556-f3" n="3" xml:id="d556-f3-content">
                <p>In a letter to Sherwood Waldron, dated June 9, 1954, Ambassador Willauer stated
                    in part the following: “There is no question in my mind that international
                    Communism is in effective control in Guatemala and that the very serious labor
                    disputes which are going on currently in Honduras are in large measure
                    attributabale to Communist influence.” (Princeton University Library, Willauer
                    papers)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
